stnsd serves users, groups and their SSH public keys over the STNS v1 HTTP
API, reading them from a TOML file.  Clients resolve accounts against it
through nsswitch, and sshd fetches authorized keys from it.

It is a second implementation of the API upstream STNS defines, in C and with
no dependency beyond libc.  The configuration file is the same one, and a test
suite serves the same file from both servers and compares every answer.

Only the TOML backend is implemented: no LDAP, no Redis and no etcd.  TLS,
including requiring client certificates, is configured with the same keys
upstream uses.
